            </div>

            <div class="about-body">
                <section>
                    <h2>The name</h2>
                    <p>Play in Traffic is what these apps help you do: run, ride, and walk through your city. We tried more polished names, but none of them were as honest, and none would make your mom smirk when she thought you weren't looking.</p>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h2>Who's building this</h2>
                    <p>Play in Traffic is built by Alec Singleton, a product and engineering leader in Toronto with a background in health tech, wearable hardware, and connected systems.</p>
                    <p>These apps started as solutions to his own problems: wanting a new running route without planning one, wanting to bike somewhere without gambling on infrastructure, and wanting a better walk than the same three blocks on autopilot. Other people had the same problems, so here we are.</p>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h2>What we make</h2>
                    <p>Three apps, all iOS, all free.</p>
                    <p><a href="/random-run.html" class="app-link--run">Random Run</a> generates running routes: pick a distance, get three options, go. <a href="/bikeright.html" class="app-link--ride">BikeRight</a> finds the safest cycling route to your destination, scored by real infrastructure. <a href="/go-for-a-walk.html" class="app-link--walk">Go for a Walk</a> builds walking loops through your neighbourhood with stops for the things you like — parks, coffee, landmarks you've walked past a hundred times without noticing.</p>
                    <p>No accounts. No tracking. No ads. Your location stays on your phone. We don't want your data.</p>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h2>Made in Canada</h2>
                    <p>Play in Traffic and all of our apps are proudly made in Canada 🇨🇦. Designed, built, and tested in Toronto. Go Greenland, Slava Ukraini, America don't let us down in the midterms.</p>
                </section>
